"Legend\"}}],\" →\"]}]]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-text-muted text-[13px] leading-relaxed\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L4c\",null,{\"k\":\"pages.heroes.rankSentenceLead\",\"params\":{\"rank\":\"Legend\",\"name\":\"Natalia\"}}],[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-text-primary\",\"children\":[\"51.61\",\"%\"]}],[\"$\",\"$L4c\",null,{\"k\":\"pages.heroes.rankSentenceMid1\",\"params\":{\"name\":\"Natalia\",\"delta\":\"+0.50%\"}}],[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-text-primary\",\"children\":[\"0.35\",\"%\"]}],[\"$\",\"$L4c\",null,{\"k\":\"pages.heroes.rankSentenceMid2\"}],[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-text-primary\",\"children\":[\"2.19\",\"%\"]}],[\"$\",\"$L4c\",null,{\"k\":\"pages.heroes.rankSentenceAfter\",\"params\":{\"rank\":\"Legend\"}}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"article\",\"mythic\",{\"className\":\"group relative min-w-0 border border-mlbb-gold/15 bg-surface-1/40 p-3.5 pl-5 md:p-4 md:pl-6 transition-colors hover:border-mlbb-gold/30\",\"children\":[\"$L9e\",\"$L9f\",\"$La0\"]}],\"$La1\",\"$La2\"]}]\n7e:[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}]\n7f:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-4\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Natalia is not an assassin in the standard sense. She does not burst a target with a three-skill combo and recall. Her threat comes from the passive: hide in a bush without taking damage and she enters stealth, gaining a movement speed boost. Her next basic attack teleports her to behind the target, dealing bonus damage and silencing them just long enough to interrupt a cast in progress.\"}]\n80:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-5\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"That interruption is the whole plan. It is just long enough to stop the carry's first skill cast, land one or two enhanced basic attacks, and back into the nearest bush before the enemy team responds. The Hunt (her ultimate) stores two charges, each granting immediate stealth. Creep kills reduce the current charge timer by half its full value, so she rebuilds charges rapidly during jungle rotations. A clean camp clear between ganks can give back a full charge before she reaches the next sidelane.\"}]\n81:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-6\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"What this means in practice: Natalia does not feel like Fanny because she cannot fight in the open. She does not feel like Hayabusa because her kill pattern is a basic attack, not a skill rotation. She is closer to a countdown than an assassin. Every second the enemy carry spends unable to move freely is a second their damage output drops, which compounds over a full game.\"}]\n82:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-7\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"The emblem matches this pattern. Assassin Emblem with Rupture plus Master Assassin plus Killing Spree gives Adaptive Penetration on approach, 7% bonus damage when the target is isolated (which the carry almost always is when Natalia reaches them), and HP recovery plus movement speed after a kill for fast repositioning.\"}]\n83:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-2\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"The first six minutes\"]}]\n84:[\"$\",\"ol\",\"ol-0\",{\"className\":\"list-decimal list-inside text-[#9BA0B4] my-3 space-y-2 ml-2\",\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Take S1 first and clear the opening camp.\"}],\" Claw Dash at level 1 lets you clear your starting camp without taking meaningful damage if you aim through the creep cluster. The base cooldown means you have it back before you need to rotate.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-1\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Level 3 opens your first real gank window.\"}],\" Once you have S1, S2, and a Hunt charge, head to the nearest sidelane bush. Settling into the bush starts stealth passively after a moment out of combat. Pop a Hunt charge to enter stealth immediately if the natural approach is too slow. The target is whichever enemy carry is pushing past the midpoint of the lane without vision coverage.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-2\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Save one Hunt charge for the second rotation.\"}],\" Many Natalia players burn both charges on the first failed gank attempt and spend the next two minutes farming with no stealth. Treat the second charge as a reserve: use it if the first gank succeeds and you need to re-stealth for the escape, or hold it until the next rotation.\"]}],\"\\n\"]}]\n85:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-3\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"The two-item window that changes the math\"]}]\n86:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-8\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"The first item that matters is Blade of the Heptaseas. Its Ambush passive triggers when you have gone 5 seconds without dealing or taking damage: the next basic attack deals bonus physical damage and applies a 40% slow. That condition is exactly what Natalia's stealth approach already creates. You sit in the bush out of combat, walk out stealthed, and the Ambush proc rides the same auto as the back-damage bonus. The 40% slow is the real payoff: the carry cannot walk out of the follow-up after the silence ends.\"}]\n87:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-9\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Endless Battle is the second item. Its Divine Justice passive fires true damage on the next basic attack after any skill activation. Activate The Hunt (a skill), walk into the backline, and the enhanced stealth auto carries the back-damage, the Ambush burst, and the true damage proc simultaneously. The Chase Fate passive adds a movement speed burst when Divine Justice fires, which closes the final gap if the carry backpedals.\"}]\n88:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-10\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Together these two items land around the 9-to-11 minute mark on a clean jungle path. Before that point, her kill potential exists but is not reliable against targets with any defense investment. After that point, a squishy carry without defensive items can be deleted in two or three enhanced autos within the Smoke Bomb window.\"}]\n89:[\"$\",\"$La3\",null,{\"slot\":\"7246933188\",\"variant\":\"in-article\",\"className\":\"my-8\"}]\n8a:[[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-0\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"Teamfight positioning: let the front go first\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"The reflexive play when a teamfight breaks out is to immediately pop a Hunt charge and dive toward the lowest-HP enemy. That reflex costs games.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-1\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"The correct sequence: let your tank or support initiate. Wait until at least one CC ability connects on the enemy frontline. Then enter stealth from a bush on the flanking side, walk past the fight, and reach the carry before anyone notices you moved. The carry is focused on the teamfight in front of them and is not checking the flank.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-2\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Three rules that override most teamfight instincts:\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"ol\",\"ol-0\",{\"className\":\"list-decimal list-inside text-[#9BA0B4] my-3 space-y-2 ml-2\",\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Never enter a teamfight without a stealth entry.\"}],\" An open Natalia in a teamfight has no dodge tool, no tank stats, and no escape. If you arrive with both Hunt charges spent and no bush nearby, stand on the edge and wait for the frontline to absorb aggro first.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-1\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Hunt charge two is the escape, not a second opener.\"}],\" Use charge one to engage. If the assassination goes clean, S1 out and retreat through the nearest bush. If you get caught mid-dive, charge two is what gets you to cover before the CC chain finishes. Spending both charges in a single fight sequence leaves you with no stealth re-entry until a full recharge cycle passes.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-2\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Smoke Bomb goes up after the stealth auto lands, not before.\"}],\" S2 blocks basic attacks. Activate it the moment the carry starts autoing back, not during the approach. Early activation burns the basic-attack immunity window on your walk-up instead of on the moment the carry tries to auto you down.\"]}],\"\\n\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-3\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"One support edge case worth knowing: Angela can attach to Natalia and teleport in during a stealth approach, adding a shield and slow the moment the silence fires. If Angela is your support, coordinate the engage timing because the teleport animation is visible and tips off the enemy team.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-1\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"Itemization: three locked slots, two conversations\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-4\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"The locked slots are Retribution (required for jungle; upgrade to Ice Retribution when it evolves, since stealing enemy movement speed on cast is what pins a target for the follow-up), Blade of the Heptaseas, and Endless Battle. Those three are not situational.\"}],\"\\n\",\"$La4\",\"\\n\",\"$La5\",\"\\n\",\"$La6\",\"\\n\",\"$La7\",\"\\n\",\"$La8\",\"\\n\",\"$La9\",\"\\n\",\"$Laa\",\"\\n\",\"$Lab\",\"\\n\",\"$Lac\",\"\\n\",\"$Lad\",\"\\n\",\"$Lae\",\"\\n\",\"$Laf\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb0\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb1\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb2\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb3\"]\n8b:[\"$\",\"$Lb4\",null,{\"heroName\":\"Natalia\"}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"8c:[\"$\",\"$L6a\",\"mathilda\",{\"href\":\"/heroes/mathilda\",\"className\":\"group block\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"relative bg-surface-4 border border-mlbb-gold/20 overflow-hidd